/-!
# Module comparisons for the characteristic-two block sieve

The source input retains the actual Sylow subgroup, residual and normal
closure, the marked S₃ × S₃ action, and the two embedding alternatives,
including the exchanged component product. The local component orbit embeds
in both the internal H-module and the local C.2.7 omega module. Its inclusion
in the omega module intertwines the actions of the same intrinsic core quotient.

The alternating-five calculation gives a cubic element fixing the Sylow
fixed space of its natural section, including nonsplit central extensions.
The actual source Sylow centralizer excludes this section once its embedding
and equivariant map are constructed.

This is not yet the complete block sieve. The full C.2.7 alternative
comparison, transport from an A₅-block to that section, binary L₄/L₅
exclusion, and the C.1.34 SL₃ exclusions remain necessary before concluding
`ExchangedL2Block`. No configuration-specific classification or Borel
placement is an input to the results published here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), C.1.34,
C.2.7, and the characteristic-two paragraph of 15.4.20, printed p.1164.
-/
